<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slobodan Milošević</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a>–<a href="/years/2006">2006</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Slobodan Milošević was a Serbian politician who rose through the League of Communists to become president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1989 and of the Federal Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> from 1997 to 2000. His Serbian nationalist policies contributed to the break-up of Yugoslavia and the wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>. Ousted in 2000, he was handed to the Hague tribunal for war crimes and died in custody before a verdict.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slobodan-milosevic.jpg" alt="Slobodan Milošević" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stevan Kragujević · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stevan_Kragujevi%C4%87,_Slobodan_Milo%C5%A1evi%C4%87,_portret.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
